if you're curious about my to-do lists  my weekly schedule and my monthly goals  i'm going to share them with you today  on this video  hi i'm evan carmichael i believe in  entrepreneurs and i recently got a great  question for one of my newsletter  subscribers  love you guys dion who's asking about my  schedule and routine  dion wrote in to say hi evan thank you  for your recent emails and for your  inspirational videos which i have now  started to implement into my daily  routine awesome this brings me to a  question relating to routine and how you  organize your day  we'd love to know what your to-do list  looks like your weekly schedule your  monthly goals and beyond  i think it would help a lot of people  like myself plan their day and achieve  their goals in a workable format if you  were to share how you plan  hope that makes sense dion so this is a  great question let's start with the  to-do lists  so with my to-do list i use two systems  tools  one is my email and one is evernote  email i'll use  for email obviously when somebody emails  me something  and i need to review it i'll usually  give it a star i use gmail you can start  and then i'll come back to it on monday  will be my time i have a chunk of time  set to be able to manage those tasks i  don't have a set time of the day where i  do  email from my general inbox and so i'm  doing email typically from my tablet  when i'm waiting in line or i'm outside  or whatever when i have down time and  traveling  that's when i'll check my email and it's  not always conducive to reviewing  documents and doing kind of the bigger  projects  and so i set aside a specific time for  that and i'll just start  when i know i have to come back to it  i'll also use email for the videos  so in my morning schedule i'm checking  my youtube channel looking the comments  that you guys have  and if i promise somebody i'm going to  make them a video often i'll say hey  this is a great question i'll make a  video reply for you then i will  send myself an email and copy and paste  that in and then on wednesday which is  video day  i'll look at all those emails and start  making videos to answer those questions  for everything else in terms of to-do  lists i use evernote  and that's where it's not reactionary  right the other ones were reactionary  where i'm getting an email or i'm  getting a comment  here is more purposeful planning where  i'm making a list of things that i need  to do  and i love evernote for that it's easy  to update and i have access to it  on my phone tablet computer laptop  everything  uh and what i'll do is i'll just make  different folders for each of the main  things that i'm working on and so  i have in my weekly schedule set time to  do set projects  and when it's time for that project to  open up i'll go to my evernote folder  and see all the things that i have to do  i usually have a  to-do list at the top in each folder  of the kind of priority things i need to  get done and then  ideas below right if i have an idea for  something  i'll just add it to that evernote file  so i'm not you know staying awake late  at night trying to remember and hope i  don't forget it for the next day  but it may not be a priority like i got  to get working on this right now  so when i'm starting up whatever task  i'll load the evernote file see what's  most important  and if i finish it then i can start  working on the other ideas that i came  up with  the next question was about my weekly  schedule so my mornings usually start  the same way i will wake up i'll have my  lentils i will  write down three things i'm grateful for  i will check my youtube comments and my  social media comments  i will also check my email folder from  my vips  which will be my family my staff  and the people in my movement coaching  program  and get back to those people pretty  quickly  then everything else is different  depending on the day  and i'm a huge believer in chunking  similar tasks together and not being  bombarded  uh and being super reactionary i believe  in really trying to be proactive in  scheduling your week to get  what you want to get done done so monday  is my get stuff done for the weekday  and that's usually starts with  me look at all of the things that i  start during the week right all those  emails that i put a star  attached to i'll look through those and  get those done so reviewing documents  getting back to emails  i will plan out the facebook campaigns  and the twitter campaigns for the week  my team will put together pictures and  things for me to approve i don't  actually design anything but it's more  you know anything going out has my name  on it so i want to make sure that it's  been approved and i like it  so i'll look at all the stuff that  they've sent me and just  it's it's admin day you know let's get  all the stuff done  for the week day and so i've divided my  day into  three chunks the first chunk is just  doing that stuff  the second chunk is thinking about my  authors i have a website where authors  can contribute content and so  i'll spend in each chunk an hour and a  half and that second chunk i'm worried  about my website  and seo stuff and author feature  requests  and any issues that i need to deal with  around that looking at the new backend  that we're working on and so on  and then the last chunk on that monday  is going to be  about my zuga guides and expanding them  and adding more to them and promoting  them and anything related to  the zuga guides happens at that time so  why it's great is because  you know people my team might email me  and say hey here's something new for the  author back-end or here's something new  for the zooka guys that i want you to  check out and if i just  responded to it right then quickly right  away it's great i guess for my team that  they have a fast answer  but it kills my time and productivity  because now i'm just being reactionary  to what they're sending me  so instead i save it you know to the  folder and know that hey on  on monday i have time for this i'm going  to look look at it  and i'm going to get back to you and so  that frees up the rest of my week to do  other things  tuesday is my writing and researching  day so i'm writing the book that could  be where i'm spending my time  researching writing for the book  now i'm spending a lot of time on my  youtube videos and researching the  famous entrepreneurs and finding clips  and now that i have a system for that  i'm going to try to involve my team  more into it because it's super taxing  it takes me the whole day tuesday  to uh find all that information to make  the videos and i'm hoping that that can  be now delegated and i can go back to  writing my book  so anything related to research or  writing or  if i'm asked to write something for an  for an article or  a guest post somewhere that'll all fall  under my tuesday category and i  book off the whole day to be able to  free up my time to do that wednesday's  video day so  today is wednesday i don't know when the  video is going live but today actually  is wednesday  and uh i you know have the mindset now  where hey i gotta be  i gotta be enthusiastic i gotta be  exciting you know monday tuesday might  be the  i don't need to talk to anybody i can  just sit there and work and now  wednesday is more extrovert itself  and uh answering your questions and i'll  make 13 videos  uh a week typically and record them and  send them off to my  editor christina to put together for you  thursday is my public facing day that's  when all the meetings happen so meetings  phone calls google plus hangouts  uh media uh corporate initiatives things  that i'm working on where i need to talk  to you  somebody else that's outside my company  that's not an email happens on thursdays  so  i try to line up back-to-back meetings  if i'm meeting somebody  it's usually at a local whole foods cafe  and then i line up back-to-back  calls and hangouts i find with the  meetings i give people a two hour window  on a thursday so i don't know exactly  what it is i want to say it's thursday  from like 11 to 1  would be meetings face to face and then  i give them the time slot and they can  either book for this week or next week  or the week after and  usually because my schedule fills up  they're looking at three or four weeks  out but it saves so much time of having  to go back and forth and back and forth  this time this time this time work and  then the afternoon is gonna be all phone  calls and and hangouts  and or skype calls or whatever um those  are all again back to back to back to  back to back there's a little bit of  travel time obviously to get from whole  foods to back here  um but again it works and and i enjoy it  and  it's my public facing day it's the day i  have my radio show and basically  anything where i am  out talking to people is for the most  part on that thursday  and then friday there's nothing  scheduled friday is maybe my travel  day if i'm going to an event friday  could be a project day friday  uh jason might come over and we'll work  on something together friday is  super buffer day and i find people  often pack so much in that they have  zero buffer time  and you get stressed out and you go  don't get your stuff done  and so i find that by packing everything  at the start monday is intense right  mondays everything for the week  done if i only had to work monday i  could get everything i needed for the  week done  to run my business and then that gives  me the time to actually go and do  other projects that i'm excited about so  i find having that buffer at the end  super helpful and sometimes i use it and  sometimes i don't  and just depends on what's happening in  my life and my business and then in  terms of monthly goals i  check a number of stats religiously  every month when midnight hits on the  first of every month  i have an excel file full of all these  things that i track  uh things like on my youtube channel how  many views how many subscribers  i'll check how many people on my  newsletter list i'll check how many  sales we made i'll check how many  uh web visitors we had to our website  and  some of the data is immediately  actionable and others i just keep just  just to track and know the biggest goal  i'm working on right now  is i want to be the number one youtuber  at the agency  that i'm at so i'm represented by a  talent agency and  they represent experts who are off you  know delivering their expertise and all  sorts of different formats  and i want to be the number one youtuber  at the agency it's a goal i set  uh when i first joined about a year and  a half ago and i am the number two  youtuber  and i'm like this close this close i've  had months where i've passed and then go  down and pass  so the challenge is you know i'm growing  i love you guys for all the  for all the love and the comments and  the traction and the sharing  but the number one person is growing too  so it's not it's a moving target  so i want to be consistently number one  and that's my biggest  goal at the moment i find having that  competition  that's a friendly competition you know  i'm friendly with the other person  but i find having that competition kind  of helps drive me a little bit more  so those are my to-do lists my weekly  schedule  the things that i look at monthly and my  goals i'd love to know  i'd love to know from you guys what the  most important  tool is that you find helpful in your  business  leave in the comments below i want to  see if i'm missing something and there's  a blind spot  that i have your favorite tool that  helps you run your business leave in the  comments below  thank you guys so much for watching if  you liked the video you want to see more  don't forget to subscribe to the channel  and the newsletter  continue to believe and i'll see you  soon

